# Agent efficiency
- Start with the smallest relevant file set. Expand only when evidence requires it.
- Do not repeatedly scan the whole repository for a focused task.
- Prefer targeted search, symbols, diffs, and referenced files over bulk reading.
- Do not load large historical prompt/spec files unless the task depends on them.
- Keep a single task focused; do not silently turn a bug fix into a broad refactor.
- Use inexpensive/fast models for mechanical edits, CSS tweaks, searches and summaries when model choice is available.
- Escalate reasoning/model capability for ambiguous architecture, difficult debugging, security-sensitive changes, or when a cheaper attempt fails.
- Avoid repeating the same large task across multiple premium models merely to bypass usage limits.
- Summarize findings before expanding scope.